From 4f3b98631848f605c898594d5ed1566e48793d31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:18:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 068/168] mfd: mtk-spmi-pmic: Complete a pending RCS request at
 probe

An SPMI PMIC raises its interrupts as RCS requests, and sends no further
request until the host writes RCS_IRQ_DONE. The bootloader can hand over
with a request outstanding: on the Jolla Phone (MT6858 with MT6363),
SPMI-M's SLV_7_4_EINT latch reads 0x4 for SID 4 when Linux starts. The
arbiter driver clears that latch at probe, but nothing completes the
request on the PMIC side, so the MT6363 never raises another one and its
keys stay silent.

Write RCS_IRQ_DONE once the interrupts are masked and cleared, as the
downstream driver does at probe.
---
 drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c b/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c
index f1b0b3eb8..8ce15dd18 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/mtk-spmi-pmic.c
@@ -342,6 +342,11 @@ static int mtk_spmi_pmic_irq_init(struct device *dev, struct regmap *regmap,
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Complete a request left pending at boot, or the PMIC sends no more */
+	ret = regmap_write(regmap, MTK_SPMI_PMIC_RCS_IRQ_DONE, 1);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Cannot complete the RCS request\n");
+
 	pmic->dom = irq_domain_create_tree(fwnode, &mtk_spmi_pmic_irq_domain_ops, pmic);
 	if (!pmic->dom)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENOMEM, "Cannot create IRQ domain\n");
